# Story: someone quits Arbor, clicks the music player, and starts Arbor again. With everything showing there is no room for the player, so it is a
# tile; it has the keyboard, so it is let be where it stands (QUESTIONS Q16). Whoever asks Arbor what it believes is told so: a window in full
# view that Arbor called hidden looked like a fault to everybody who held `arborctl state` against the screen.
quiet
set makeRoom false
open Music
open Safari
open Notes
open Mail
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
dock 104 beside 102 bottom
# Of its half of 702 points 202 are left: too narrow to show any window in.
resize 101 right -500
wait 3
expect tile 101
expect hidden 101
relaunch quit
focus 101
relaunch start
wait 3
# Docked, its tile keeps its place, and it is in view.
expect docked 101
expect tile 101
expect visible 101
expect focused 101
state
expect replied 101 is let be where it stands
ascii
expect replied let be: w101 Music
# A layout that somebody asks for ends it: a window like any other again, out of view behind its tile, and said to be.
relayout
wait 3
expect hidden 101
ascii
expect replied hidden: w101 Music
